<title>SPAIN: Spain's Repsol acquired 60 percent of Peru'S Solgas.</title>
<headline>Spain's Repsol acquired 60 percent of Peru'S Solgas.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Repsol Confirmed on Monday it had acquired a 60 percent stake in Peru's Solgas for $39 million.</p>
<p>A press statement said the remaining 40 percent is owned by the Grupo Day, Ortuzar y Gruenberg and Chilean group Lipigas.</p>
<p>The note added that Solgas is the main operator in Peru's market of petrol gas, with a market share of 40 percent.</p>
<p>Repsol started its operation in Peru in 1993, and is now planning to invest in the country, together with its partners, $117 million, the note said.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
